  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Based on their acid-base characteristics oxides are classified as acidic or basic. An oxide that combines with water to give an acid is termed as an acidic oxide. The oxide that gives a base in water is known as a basic oxide.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>10</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>5</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are acidic oxides.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NO</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>CO</mi></math> are neutral oxides.</p></blockquote>",
